[Music]  have you heard of Bali have you tried it  if you have watched my 11 hike up fruits  you should be eating you would have  learned that if this underrated green  it's one of the world's oldest super  foods and it's loaded with all the  essential nutrients Valley water is an  incredible drink which our ancestors  included in their daily diet when I was  growing up I remember drinking barley  water on a regular basis if you can swim  badly on a regular basis it will keep  your colon and intestines happy it will  control your blood cholesterol levels  you will maintain your skin elasticity  and you will strengthen your immune  system plus is extremely affordable Bali  contains about 62% of dietary fiber and  you will be getting 20 to 25% of your  daily fiber in just one serving the best  way to use Bali is to simply treat it  like rice oats or any other greens you  can make stir-fry bali rice risotto  steel or soups or toss it into salads so  I'm gonna share with you four really  simple recipes which you can make for  breakfast lunch and also dinner let's  start with breakfast we got a barley  porridge on the menu it's really simple  in a small pot combine quarter cup of  pearl Valley with 3/4 cup of water and  bring it to a boil lower the heat and  simmer for about 20 to 30 minutes until  the water has been absorbed and barley  is completely soft then stir in about  half a cup of milk and allow it to  simmer very quickly until you get your  desired consistency remove from heat  so I've served my with one sliced banana  1 tablespoon of apricot seeds and about  1 teaspoon of chia seeds you can choose  to drizzle with a little bit of honey  having a fiber rich breakfast will keep  you going till lunchtime  so each Bowl has about 460 calories the  chewy and tender texture of barley is  very similar to oatmeal plus it is very  easy to make  so you can stop your breakfast and  replace odds with barley  let's make lunch I have barley and  beaded salad on my menu for this recipe  you can use barley as a replacement for  rice couscous or quinoa salads are my go  to lunch because most of the ingredients  do not require cooking so what I've used  are one and a half cup of cooked barley  two cups of baby spinach 1/2 a cup of  public cabbage 2 bits cooked and sliced  about quarter cup of fresh mint leaves 2  tablespoons of feta cheese cubed 1 tbsp  of dried cranberries 1 tbsp of apricot  seeds about 1/2 a tbsp of olive oil 2  tablespoons of lemon juice and 1 tsp of  honey it's so simple all you have to do  is assemble all the vegetables together  then drizzle with olive oil lemon juice  and honey and serve you're getting the  earthy flavor from the beets combined  with the chewy body texture crunchiness  from the spinach and cabbage and tangy  nurse from the feta cheese it is so  simple it's delicious and is so colorful  and each serving only has about 314  calories lunch is about keeping it  simple quick and healthy so try this  recipe out and choose any other  vegetables of your choice and with the  leftover body here's another really  simple lunch you can put together stir  fry barley rice with on the rise of  course what I've used are 1 and 1/2 cups  of cooked barley 1 medium carrot diced  about half a cup of mushrooms sliced 1/2  a red bell pepper diced 1 and a half  cups of cabbage shredded one whole  zucchini diced half a head of broccoli  cut into florets 2 cloves of garlic  crushed 1 tablespoon of olive oil 2  tablespoons of soy sauce and salt and  pepper to taste in a pan heat oil over  medium-high heat then stir in all the  vegetables garlic mushrooms carrots  zucchinis red bell pepper  broccoli and cabbage saute them very  quickly for three to four minutes then  mix in the barley soy sauce and also  salt and pepper to taste  toss all the ingredients thoroughly  until they are well combined  this dish is delicious warm or chilled  and each serving only has about 314  calories packing in lots of vegetables  is the key to keeping your fried rice  healthy plus you're getting your rainbow  I wanted as something comforting for  dinner so I'm making barley and beef  stew for this recipe you'll need 1/2 a  cup of pearl barley about 300 grams of  beef ribs let's prep all the vegetables  chop up one carrot a cup of celery a cup  of mushrooms and 1 onion in a pot melt  about half a tablespoon of butter over  medium high heat then sear the beef  pieces you want to season it with a  little bit of salt and pepper set aside  now in the same pot add in the chopped  onions and saute until fragrant and  slightly Brown just for about 5 to 6  minutes then stir in the mushrooms and  cook very quickly and is slightly tender  for about 2 to 3 minutes then add the  beef back into the pot add in about 2  cups of water and sprinkle with half a  teaspoon of dried basil then allow the  beef to gently simmer under low heat  until very tender for about 1 hour once  the beef is tender add in the remaining  ingredients barley celery and carrots  continue to cook all the ingredients  until they are very tender for at least  45 to 60 minutes now if you like your  meat a falling off the bone then cook  for another additional hour serve hot H  serving has about 418 calories and this  is a one pot dish so you can double up  the ingredients and cook it for a huge  family you can even choose to serve it  as a starter so try all these different  Valley recipes out let me know which is  your favorite in the comments  if you haven't yet tried Valley you have  to give this super grain a chance you  will love it you will love the chewy and  tender texture of Barney don't forget to  snap pictures tag me at Jonas official  and hashtag it chase your recipes to  like this video share this video and  subscribe to my youtube channel for a  lot more healthy and delicious recipes  do check out my workout challenges as  well okay so eat well stay healthy stay  active and all the best

